                "Rise of Absentee Landlords: Commercial moneylenders, merchants, and banyas from Calcutta bought auctioned estates, residing in luxury in Calcutta while leaving revenue extraction to ruthless managers.",
                "Extreme Sub-Infeudation (Patni System): Zamindars created multiple intermediary tenure holders (Patnidars, Dar-Patnidars, Seh-Patnidars); each layer extorted the cultivator, creating an unsustainable pyramid of parasites.",
                "Pauperization of the Bengal Ryot: Cultivators were reduced from hereditary owners to tenants-at-will, subjected to illegal cesses (Abwabs), arbitrary rent increases, and eviction."
