                "Key Strachey recommendations: Free relief for the infirm, work relief for the able-bodied, creation of a permanent Famine Relief and Insurance Fund (Rs 1.5 crore annually), and formulation of the Provisional Famine Code (1883).",
                "3. Lyall Commission (1898): Appointed under Sir James Lyall after the 1896–97 famine; recommended expanding irrigation works and providing gratuitous relief to purdahnashin women.",
                "4. MacDonnell Commission (1901): Appointed by Lord Curzon under Sir Antony MacDonnell after the 1899–1900 famine; introduced the principle of 'moral strategy'—early government intervention before peasants exhaust their savings.",
                "MacDonnell Commission recommended the establishment of an Agricultural Bank, appointment of a Famine Commissioner in affected provinces, and non-official relief cooperation."
