                "During the 1857 Revolt, the telegraph saved the British Empire; as a captured sepoy remarked: 'The electric wire has strangled us!'",
                "Modern Postal System: Post Office Act of 1854 established a uniform, low postage rate of half an anna (1/2 anna) for letters weighing up to 1/2 tola across all India, regardless of distance.",
                "First postage stamps were issued in Karachi in 1852 (the famous 'Scinde Dawk') and nationwide in 1854.",
                "Public Works Department (PWD): Dalhousie created a separate civilian PWD in 1854, taking public infrastructure out of military control.",
                "Irrigation Works: Notable colonial canal projects included the Upper Ganges Canal (engineered by Sir Proby Cautley, opened 1854), Bari Doab Canal (Punjab), and Godavari/Krishna delta anicuts (engineered by Sir Arthur Cotton).",
                "Irrigation was heavily starved of funding compared to railways: for every pound spent on canals, the government spent over twenty pounds on railways."
